issues.failure_explanation:
The lemma asserts that $\{  s{s}_{j,j} \mm 	U_{:,j} \}_{j=1}^r$ is a minimal generating set for the image. The proof establishes spanning, but the minimality step is invalid twice over: the displayed computation equals $ s{s}_{j,j}^\CT \mm  s{s}_{j,j} 
eq  s{0}$ regardless of any $k$-wise terms, so it does not even yield the claimed existence of $k$ with $ s{s}_{j,j} \mm \vec{\matW}_k^\CT \mm 	U_{:,j} 
eq  s{0}$; and even granting that such a $k$ exists for each $j$, a single $k$ could witness all $j$, so $r' \geq r$ does not follow. The statement is true (if a proper subset generated the image, writing $ s{s}_{j_0} \mm 	U_{:,j_0} = \sum_{j 
eq j_0}  s{z}_j \mm  s{s}_j \mm 	U_{:,j}$ and left-multiplying by $	U_{:,j_0}^\CT$ forces $ s{s}_{j_0} =  s{0}$ by unitarity), but the printed proof does not establish it.

